{
  "pct": {
    "primary": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.blue.600}"
    },
    "primary-hover": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.blue.700}"
    },
    "primary-active": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.blue.800}"
    },
    "on-primary": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.0}"
    },
    "surface": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.0}"
    },
    "surface-100": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.100}"
    },
    "text": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.900}"
    },
    "text-muted": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.700}"
    },
    "border": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.200}"
    },
    "border-strong": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.500}"
    },
    "$comment-danger": "`danger` has no `on-danger` pair, because in this library it is not a SURFACE: it paints the message text and the error state's border, nothing else. Until A12 the pair hung here declared and used by no token and no stylesheet — that is, it looked like coverage that did not exist. It will return with the first component painting a background with the error colour (toast, badge), and then it will show in the diff.",
    "danger": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.red.600}"
    },
    "focus-ring": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.blue.500}"
    },
    "surface-disabled": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.surface-100}"
    },
    "text-disabled": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "{pct.slate.500}"
    },
    "shadow-panel": {
      "$type": "shadow",
      "$value": "0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.14)"
    }
  }
}
